 * 
 * @section dev_reg_class_summary Summary
 * 
 * Device registry class diagram shows class inheritance hierarchy and dependencies for the 
 * public device registration interface, which is accessible via the Lime Suite NG library API.
 *
 * In Lime Suite NG each unique SDR device is classified under a unique device factory (otherwise
 * known as a device class). Each unique device factory is derived from the base device factory
 * class ``DeviceRegistryEntry``, which acts as an interface class. The base device factory class
 * declares the base device enumeration and registration functions, which are overriden with 
 * specific implementations of each unique device factory. Additionally, the base device factory
 * interface class defines a specific implementation of registration of all unique device 
 * factories in to a single device factory map with a common access interface.
 * 
 * The public device enumeration and registration interface class ``DeviceRegistry`` uses the 
 * base device factory interface and device factory map to access all available implementations
 * of device enumeration or registration functions to detect all supported SDR devices.
 * 
 * Both the public registration interface and the device factory classes depend on ``DeviceHandle`` 
 * storage class class and ``SDRDevice`` interface class. All implementations of device enumeration 
 * function return device connection information via the ``DeviceHandle`` type object with specific 
 * device connection information, while the ``SDRDevice`` provides a universal SDR device control
 * interface upon successfull registration of the SDR device.
 * 
 * @subsection dev_reg_class_legend Diagram legend
 * 
 * Link definitions:
 * 
 * - Solid line with a transparet arrow head body - Inheritance
 * - Dotted line with simple arrow head - Dependency
 * 
 */